el Valley is a broad fertile plain in northern Israel, between the hills of Galilee and Samaria, running from Mount Carmel towards the Jordan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/jezzailchi"><span class="enc-name">Jezzailchi</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Jezzailchis were soldiers armed with the jezail, a long-barrelled musket used in Iran, Afghanistan and Central Asia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jezzar-pasha"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jezzar-pasha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jezzar Pasha</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Jezzar Pasha, Ahmad Pasha al-Jazzar, was an Ottoman governor of Bosnian origin who ruled from Acre as governor of Sidon from 1775 until his death in 1804.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/jhajjar"><span class="enc-name">Jhajjar</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Jhajjar is a town in Haryana, India, west of Delhi, and the headquarters of Jhajjar district.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jhala"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jhala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jhala (clan)</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Jhala are a Rajput clan of western India whose chiefs ruled several princely states of Kathiawar in Gujarat, notably Dhrangadhra, Wankaner, Limbdi and Sayla, as…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/jhalawad"><span class="enc-name">Jhalawad</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Jhalawad was one of the historic regions, or prants, of Kathiawar in Gujarat, western India, in the north-east of the peninsula near the Little Rann of Kutch.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jhalrapatan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jhalrapatan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jhalrapatan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Jhalrapatan is a town in the Jhalawar district of south-eastern Rajasthan, India, beside the later capital of Jhalawar State.</span></a></li></ul>
